  "question": {
    "text": "A TV transmitting antenna is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>98</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> high and the receiving antenna is at the ground level. If the radius of the earth is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the surface area covered by the transmitting antenna is&nbsp;approximately:"
